@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Adapted from reviewed presentation sources: W3-10/11/12/12a/13/13a; retry identity and independent stale fences
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 17
skinparam ClassStereotypeFontSize 15
skinparam NoteFontSize 16
skinparam LegendFontSize 15
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 165
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 24
hide footbox
hide circle
title UC-4 · retry identity and current-attempt fences
top to bottom direction
class "Job\nprocessing.models" as J <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + id: UUID
 + current_attempt_id: UUID
 + status: str
 + deleted_at: datetime | None
}
class "Attempt\nprocessing.models" as A <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + id: UUID
 + job_id: UUID
 + attempt_number: int
 + lease_token: UUID | None
 + lease_expires_at: datetime | None
}
class "RetryRequest\nprocessing.models" as R <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + job_id: UUID
 + request_id: UUID
 + attempt_id: UUID
}
class "messaging\nprocessing" as M <<module>> $PROC {
 {static} - _retry_locked(session, job, request_id)
}
class "RequestKey\nmedia.models" as K <<ORM>> $MEDIA {
 + owner_id: UUID
 + operation: str
 + request_key: UUID
 + asset_id: UUID
}
class "v1_lifecycle\nmedia.services" as V <<module>> $MEDIA {
 {static} + retry(session, owner_id, asset_id, key)
}
V ..> K : public replay
V ..> M : asynchronous retry command
M ..> J : locked transition
J "1" -- "1..*" A
J "0..1" --> "1" A : current
J "1" -- "0..*" R : unique job / request
R "0..1" --> "1" A : successor
legend bottom
Selected fields. RequestKey and RetryRequest are stored in separate databases.
Public replay and successor creation have independent deduplication identities and transaction owners.
endlegend
@enduml
